cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these files, cite this release. This is the replication package
  of the paper "How much debt does money need?". Code is MIT; documentation and
  the project's stored data are CC BY 4.0; the Federal Reserve data keep their
  own terms (see LICENSE).
title: "How much debt does money need? Replication files"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Steinberger
    given-names: John Paul
abstract: >-
  Code and data that compute the transaction-based debt kernel, the least
  debt compatible with each sector's money and net financial position, for
  the United States 2001-2025, from the Federal Reserve's Financial Accounts,
  with independent checks of every stored balance sheet and of the
  transactions that reach the kernel.
keywords:
  - debt kernel
  - money
  - debt
  - sectoral balance sheets
  - financial accounts
  - flow of funds
  - stock-flow consistency
  - inside and outside money
  - money creation
  - debt reduction
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
version: "1.0.0"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24482763
repository-code: "https://github.com/vistuleB/how-much-debt"
